===========================================================================
1. (Retired 2026-10-03)
===========================================================================

This section covered the earlier Game & Watch engine, gnw.js, whose CPU
cores and speaker were ports of another emulator's sources. That file is no
longer part of this distribution: the Game & Watch emulation is this
project's own clean-room core (play/gnw/gwc-core.js) driven by the project's
own host (play/gnw/gnw-host.js). The per-title tables the host still carries
(input wiring, firmware identities) are data read from published tables, not
code (tables are data). Section numbers below are
kept so existing references to them stay valid.

The game firmware and melody firmware are not part of this distribution
either: they are Sharp mask-ROM dumps recovered from real silicon by hardware
preservationists (above all Sean Riddle,
https://seanriddle.com/gameandwatch.html) -- see NOTICE.


