19. Review scores and descriptions: LaunchBox Games Database
===========================================================================

Role     : The "Review score" line in a game's drawer and the rating on a
           game tile (metadata/*.json.gz field rs, read by gamemeta.js): the
           mean of the database users' 1 to 5 star votes and the number of
           votes, with a link to the game's page on the database's website;
           and the "About the game" text of a game no other source describes.
Source   : LaunchBox Games Database (https://gamesdb.launchbox-app.com/), by
           Unbroken Software, from its public download Metadata.zip (fetched
           2026-10-14; sha256 in WASM_Source/metadata/sources.json) and its
           public platform listings, read one page a second, for the page
           numbers the links need (WASM_Source/metadata/fetch-lb-links.mjs).
Kept     : per game only the mean rating, the vote count and the page number,
           and (since 2026-11-04) the game's description (Overview) where no
           other source has one (field d with ds "lb"; WASM_Source/metadata/
           lb-text.mjs and build.mjs). Names, alternate names and database ids
           are used only to join a record to a game and are not shipped. No
           pictures are copied.
Terms    : checked 2026-10-14 and again 2026-10-28. The database publishes no
           licence and no terms of use: its site links only to the publisher's
           privacy policy (https://www.unbrokensoftware.com/privacy/), which
           says nothing about reusing the data; the download carries no
           licence file; /terms does not exist (404); robots.txt sets no
           content signal and no disallow rule. There is no public API, so no
           API terms apply. Nothing found forbids this use.
How met  : the numbers are facts (a mean and a count), credited by name with a
           link wherever they are shown (the drawer's notes line, "Review
           scores from LaunchBox Games Database"), and each score links back
           to its source page. A description from it carries the line "The
           description is from the LaunchBox Games Database" with a link, and
           the About credits name it. Neither is covered by the CC BY-SA 4.0
           offer of the metadata packs (section 6). Shipping was approved on
           2026-10-14 (scores) and 2026-11-04 (descriptions). Builds without them: build.mjs --no-launchbox (scores) and
           --no-launchbox-text (descriptions).
If its terms change: this use is looked at again if the database publishes terms that restrict it.


